wagons were once loaded. The lone mountain looms directly north, and a
narrow trail climbs through the rocks to the dark mouth of the old mine.
Someone has scratched a warning on a boulder beside the trail. To the
northeast the southern end of the great range can be seen. The road leads
back south.
